      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, malfunctioning solenoids or sticking passages within the valve body are very likely causes for erratic pressure. Look for spikes that seem related to specific shift points; if the spikes happen randomly during cruising, suspect a pressure regulator or line restriction. A trained technician can often observe the electrical signals going to the solenoids simultaneously with the pressure spikes to confirm if a solenoid is failing to modulate pressure correctly.",
