    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "It's weird because the pressure is jumping all over the place even when the truck is just idling at a stop. It feels almost intentional, like it's not a steady mechanical failure but something intermittent and random. Any idea why it would act so erratic when there's no load on it?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Erratic pressure spikes at idle suggest a control circuit issue, as there is no load demanding high pressure. This points toward a problem with a governor, pressure relief valve, or a solenoid that is \"hunting\" for a setpoint. Intermittent electronic faults, like a failing solenoid or a low voltage issue to the control module, can manifest as these strange, seemingly intentional fluctuations even when the truck is stationary.",
